@echo off
rem On the closed-network PC, copy this to config.env and fill in the values.
rem
rem This file is not executed. tools\config_parse.py parses it, rejects keys
rem that no .bat reads, rejects CMD metacharacters in values, and writes a
rem sanitized copy the .bat files call. Every line must be one of: blank, a
rem rem comment, or set "KEY=VALUE".

rem Backend directory suffix to use: cuda | cpu
rem >>> vulkan is refused by start-llama.bat for this model. The Vulkan backend
rem >>> does not implement ggml_ssm_conv / ggml_ssm_scan for the qwen35
rem >>> architecture and corrupts state silently - upstream issue
rem >>> ggml-org/llama.cpp#19957. If CUDA fails, cpu is the only fallback.
set "LLAMA_BACKEND=cuda"

rem llama-server port. Binds to 127.0.0.1 only.
rem >>> This is the single source for the port. The bundle root's models.json is
rem >>> a template with a placeholder, and start-pi.bat / verify-offline.bat
rem >>> render home\agent\models.json from this value on every run. Do not edit
rem >>> models.json by hand - it is inside the manifest hash scope.
set "LLAMA_PORT=8080"

rem Context length (62k) of the Pi profile (start-llama.bat with no argument, one
rem slot). 63488 uses about 3.9 GiB of KV cache at f16; the default K q8_0 / V f16
rem makes it about 2.9 GiB. Only the 16 full-attention layers of qwen35 hold KV
rem that grows with context: 2 x 4 kv heads x 256 dims x ctx x 2 bytes x 16.
rem The 48 Gated DeltaNet layers keep a fixed-size state instead.
rem >>> Must be a multiple of 256: llama-server rounds n_ctx up to 256 and Pi
rem >>> would keep the smaller number. config_parse.py refuses anything else.
rem >>> This is also Pi's context window: start-pi.bat / verify-offline.bat
rem >>> render it into home\agent\models.json, so Pi compacts and caps output
rem >>> against the window the server really has.
rem >>> UD-Q5_K_M is 18.4 GiB + mmproj 0.87 GiB + about 2.9 GiB KV before compute
rem >>> buffers. It fits 3x 11GB on paper; GPU_TENSOR_SPLIT decides whether each
rem >>> card does. The KG bundle guide's larger-context tables are its own
rem >>> estimates, not measurements on this PC.
set "LLAMA_CTX=63488"

rem The exact GGUF filename inside models\.
rem >>> Bundled (2026-09-22, aligned with the closed-network KG bundle):
rem >>>   Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q5_K_M.gguf  default, 18.4 GiB (Unsloth dynamic quant,
rem >>>                               sha256 2de73110..., checked against HF)
rem >>>   Qwen3.8-27B-Q6_K.gguf       backup, 20.9 GiB - the only base with a
rem >>>                               verified LoRA adapter load (LORA_FILE)
rem >>>   Qwen3.8-27B-Q4_K_M.gguf     low-VRAM fallback, 15.7 GiB
rem >>> Switching keeps the alias, the mmproj and the pinned template
rem >>> (CHAT_TEMPLATE_FILE) - the UD-Q5_K_M file embeds a different template.
set "MODEL_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q5_K_M.gguf"

rem The model ID Pi will use. Appears under this name in /v1/models, and is
rem also what gets rendered into home\agent\models.json as the model id.
set "MODEL_ALIAS=qwen3.8-27b"

rem 3-GPU split ratio. 10,11,8 is the KG bundle's starting value: GPU0 drives
rem the display and GPU2 also hosts the bge-m3 embedding server (about 1.2 GB),
rem so both get less. Re-derive it from free VRAM measured with nvidia-smi on
rem the target PC. Blank = llama.cpp's default split. A fixed 1,1,1 is forbidden.
set "GPU_TENSOR_SPLIT=10,11,8"

rem The vision projector filename inside models\. When set, llama-server comes
rem up multimodal via --mmproj, and screenshots of error codes can be fed in as
rem images. The default is filled in here - feeding a photo of an error screen
rem on the closed-network PC is the actual intended use of this import. Leave it
rem blank only when image input is not needed or when narrowing down a problem
rem to text-only.
set "MMPROJ_FILE=mmproj-Qwen3.8-27B-BF16.gguf"

rem The model ID passed to Pi. Must be in "<provider>/<MODEL_ALIAS>" form.
rem   - the <provider> prefix must match the providers key (local) in the bundle root's models.json.
rem   - the suffix must match MODEL_ALIAS above **character for character.**
rem config_parse.py refuses the file when the two disagree, and
rem render_models_json.py refuses to write a models.json the ID cannot resolve in.
set "PI_MODEL_ID=local/qwen3.8-27b"

rem How hard the model thinks: off | low | medium | high.
rem This is not cosmetic. The Qwen3.8 chat template inside the GGUF reads
rem   {%- set resolved_reasoning_effort = reasoning_effort|default('xhigh') %}
rem so a request that carries no reasoning_effort runs at xhigh - the template's
rem own most verbose setting - and thinking tokens count against the same output
rem budget as the answer. Pi compacts above contextWindow - 16384 (47104 with
rem the 63488 default; 16384 with the old -c 32768, where the usable answer budget
rem was roughly 12000 tokens), and an xhigh turn can still walk past it. The provider then reports finish_reason "length" and Pi prints
rem "Response was truncated before completion." and ends the turn.
rem start-pi.bat passes this value as --thinking. Leave it blank to accept the
rem bundle default (medium). Change it live inside Pi with /thinking.
set "PI_THINKING=medium"

rem The provider name Pi uses to recognize the local endpoint. This is the
rem value the bundle root's models.json declares statically, matching the
rem prefix of PI_MODEL_ID. It is for reference only - the .bat files do not
rem consume it directly.
set "PI_PROVIDER=local"

rem Max seconds to wait for the model to load. A 22.4GB Q6_K model on a slow disk
rem may need more than 600s. start-pi.bat passes this straight to wait_model.py.
set "MODEL_LOAD_TIMEOUT=600"

rem Opt-in for the cpu backend. Loading a 22.4GB model into system RAM is a
rem diagnostic move, not a fallback - a 27B dense model does not reach usable
rem speed on CPU, and a machine short of RAM or pagefile thrashes for a long
rem time instead of failing. start-llama.bat refuses LLAMA_BACKEND=cpu unless
rem this is 1.
set "ALLOW_CPU_DIAGNOSTIC=0"

rem How to run Python. If start-pi.bat / verify-offline.bat find this blank,
rem they try the bundled bin\python\python.exe first, then py -3.12, then
rem python. If none of those work, write the full path here.
rem
rem >>> Note that config.env itself is parsed by Python, and that parse runs
rem >>> before this value is known. That bootstrap always uses the bundled
rem >>> bin\python\python.exe, then py -3.12, then python.
rem >>>
rem >>> install-python-packages.bat alone is different. The embedded
rem >>> distribution has no pip and cannot install packages, so that script
rem >>> uses the **target PC's system Python 3.12** instead (py -3.12, then
rem >>> python). If a value is set here, that script uses it too, but only
rem >>> after checking it is 3.12 and that import pip works. In other words,
rem >>> if you write bin\python\python.exe here, that script stops with
rem >>> "no pip" - leave it blank or point it at a system Python 3.12 instead.
set "PYTHON_CMD="

rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem Tuning for 3x GTX 1080 Ti (Pascal 6.1, 11GB each, no NVLink) and 128GB RAM,
rem aligned with the closed-network KG bundle on 2026-09-22. Values below are
rem measured-later knobs: the rehearsal records VRAM and tokens/s for each one.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rem Flash attention: auto | off. auto probes the device and turns itself off
rem with a log line if it cannot run; llama.cpp b11010 has tile/vec kernels for
rem head size 256 on GPUs without tensor cores, so the log may read enabled.
rem off is what the KG bundle guide sets (its "FA impossible on Pascal" note
rem quotes an error message that b11010 no longer has). Rehearsal 11-2 compares
rem the two. on is refused: it skips the probe and can put the op on the CPU.
set "LLAMA_FLASH_ATTN=auto"

rem K cache type: f16 | q8_0. Since 2026-09-22 this sets the K cache only; the
rem V cache stays f16 because a quantized V cache needs flash attention, which
rem may be off. q8_0 on K saves about a quarter of the KV cache without FA.
set "LLAMA_KV_TYPE=q8_0"

rem Chat template file inside chat-templates\, passed as --chat-template-file.
rem qwen38-c3cf9e34.jinja is the original Qwen3.8 template (the one inside the
rem Q6_K file) that every tool round-trip, render parity and LoRA data check
rem used. The UD-Q5_K_M file embeds an Unsloth variant instead. Blank = use the
rem template embedded in MODEL_FILE. start-pi.bat checks the server serves it.
set "CHAT_TEMPLATE_FILE=qwen38-c3cf9e34.jinja"

rem Host-RAM prompt cache in MiB (llama-server --cache-ram). With one slot, a
rem subagent turn evicts the main session's KV state; this keeps it in RAM so
rem the next turn does not re-prefill the whole history, which is the slowest
rem step on Pascal. 128GB RAM minus the page-cached model leaves plenty; blank
rem keeps the llama.cpp default of 8192.
set "LLAMA_CACHE_RAM_MIB=32768"

rem Speculative decoding with the model's own MTP layer: 0 | 1. Off until the
rem rehearsal A/B shows a gain - on this hybrid model the server rolls the
rem recurrent state back through checkpoints, which costs time on Pascal.
set "LLAMA_SPEC_MTP=0"

rem Physical batch size for prompt processing (llama-server -ub), 16 to 1024
rem (the logical batch -b is fixed at 1024). 256 is the KG bundle's value: the
rem 248,320-entry vocabulary makes the logits buffer large at 512. If long
rem prompts reset the display driver (Windows TDR, "display driver stopped
rem responding"), try 128. Smaller is slower prefill but shorter GPU steps.
set "LLAMA_UBATCH=256"

rem LoRA adapter file name inside lora\ (a GGUF adapter converted with
rem llama.cpp convert_lora_to_gguf.py). Blank = base model only; clearing it is
rem the rollback. After setting it, run verify-offline.bat - an adapter that
rem breaks the tool round-trip must not stay active.
rem >>> Only allowed with MODEL_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-Q6_K.gguf, the base whose
rem >>> adapter load was verified. config_parse.py refuses it on UD-Q5_K_M until
rem >>> that base is verified too.
set "LORA_FILE="

rem Adapter strength, greater than 0 and at most 2. 1.0 is the trained scale.
set "LORA_SCALE=1.0"

rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem Learning without training (pi-extensions\learning.ts): learned rules from past
rem sessions are injected every turn, the model saves them with remember_rule,
rem and proven multi-step procedures become one-call skill tools after /skill-approve.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rem Automatic reflection: 0 | 1. After an interactive task that used 8 or more tool
rem calls and finished normally (at most once every 30 minutes), Pi reviews it and
rem saves up to 2 project rules / 1 pending skill. Each reflection is an extra model
rem turn, which takes minutes on 3x 1080 Ti - set 0 to keep only the manual /reflect.
set "LEARNING_AUTO_REFLECT=1"

rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem pi-subagents tool switch: 1 | 0. The definitions of the three tools this
rem package adds (subagent, bg_wait, subagent_supervisor) are 23.6k characters
rem of each request. Measured on the first request only, with the bundled
rem pi.exe against a stub server in -p mode: 60,235 characters with them and
rem 36,592 without through start-pi.bat (46,586 and 22,943 with pi.exe alone).
rem The share depends on the setup and shrinks as the history grows. What it
rem is worth in tokens and prefill seconds on 3x 1080 Ti has not been measured
rem - rehearsal 11-17 runs both settings, and the default is decided after it.
rem   1  as before: the tools are offered to the model.
rem   0  start-pi.bat adds --exclude-tools for those three names. The package,
rem      its skills, prompts, commands and hooks stay; delegation and the
rem      superpowers skills that rely on it (subagent-driven-development,
rem      dispatching-parallel-agents, requesting-code-review) cannot delegate,
rem      so a review done in the same session is not an independent review.
rem With 0, start-pi.bat refuses your own --exclude-tools / -xt argument (exit
rem 12): Pi applies only the last one. To keep your own list and drop these
rem tools too, set 1 and add the three names to your list. Takes effect at the
rem next start-pi.bat.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
set "PI_SUBAGENT_TOOLS=1"

rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rem Knowledge-graph stack (closed-network KG bundle, 2026-09-22): LightRAG with
rem a local LLM server and a bge-m3 embedding server. install-kg.bat once, then
rem start-llama.bat kg, start-embedding.bat, start-lightrag.bat. The kg profile
rem uses LLAMA_PORT too, so it replaces the Pi server while it runs; start-pi.bat
rem refuses to attach to it.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rem kg profile context, shared by KG_PARALLEL slots (32768 / 4 = 8192 per slot).
rem Entity extraction is many short chunk calls, so parallel slots beat one
rem long context. kg\lightrag.env caps every request to fit one slot - change
rem both together.
set "KG_CTX=32768"
set "KG_PARALLEL=4"

rem Embedding server (start-embedding.bat): model file inside models\, port,
rem and the GPU index it runs on (passed as CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES).
set "EMBED_MODEL_FILE=bge-m3-FP16.gguf"
set "EMBED_PORT=8081"
set "EMBED_GPU=2"

rem Reranker server (start-rerank.bat): model file inside models\, port, and
rem the GPU index it runs on. bge-reranker-v2-m3 re-scores the chunks a
rem LightRAG query found; kg\lightrag.env turns it on and start-lightrag.bat
rem refuses to start while it is on and this server does not answer. It
rem shares GPU 2 with the embedding server by default - neither its VRAM nor
rem its latency has been measured on the target PC yet. The three server
rem ports (LLAMA_PORT, EMBED_PORT, RERANK_PORT) must all differ.
set "RERANK_MODEL_FILE=bge-reranker-v2-m3-Q8_0.gguf"
set "RERANK_PORT=8082"
set "RERANK_GPU=2"
